# Not an optimisation. BuildKit transfers only the files a COPY asks for, and
# the Dockerfile asks for four by name plus src/ and assets/.
#
# It is a guard. The day a `COPY . .` appears, or a `.env` or a local `dist/` is
# sitting in the working directory when the release workflow runs, this is what
# keeps it out of an image that gets pushed to two registries.
#
# `assets/` is deliberately absent from this list: the fonts in it are the one
# thing the image needs at runtime that the build does not produce.
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.github/
.env*
*.log
tmp-check/
